{
 "_about": "The valley woodland (LAYOUT valley 'woodland', 320 x 576 world px) at density 2, drawn by the kit from this plan and the woodland biome. Its geometry is today's 1x woodland (scripts/art/valley_zones.py woodland), read call by call, so the walk mask, the stands, the ports and the forager's round stay exactly as they are: the objects keep their ids, boxes and feet, and the water and rock footprints (water_rle, rock_rle: per row the runs [x0, x1) in world px) are the 1x's own. The 1x zone stays for density 1. Rendered by: python3 scripts/art/native_zones.py Density 3 (25 Oct): log-1 lies 8 px further west so its end no longer runs into tree-4's trunk (walk.txt in game/zones/woodland blocks its new cells), and a worn spur leads from the path to the bench. The bushes, hollies and brambles come in variants (bush_b, bush_c, holly_b, bramble_b: other sizes, shapes and greens), and pine-1, pine-2 and pine-7 stand 10 px lower so more of their crowns show under the top edge. wood-14 (a sapling) stands 18 px east and wood-26 (an oak) 41 px west so their crowns are not hidden behind tree-4 and the willow (check:kit 'every trunk shows its crown'). wood-39 (a beech wholly behind wood-44 and pine-4, only its pale trunk showing) is gone; the clump keeps its blocked cells. wood-5 (a birch) stands 14 px west, out from under wood-4's crown. pine-7 and pine-1 stand a further 20 and 14 px lower and wood-6, wood-16 and wood-19 9 px further in, so at least 70 % of every crown lies inside the zone (review:scene crown_cut). wood-11 and tree-8 (birches whose crowns ran into the oaks' crowns, so their pale trunks read as bare poles) are a holly and a bush now, and wood-44 (a slim beech in the clump) an oak (check:kit's slim-tree rule). tree-5 (a birch) stands 14 px further south so its crown no longer hangs over the river's bank. wood-26 (an oak) stands 16 px further north so its trunk is off the path's edge (#288 review S7), and wood-25 (a beech whose crown that oak and wood-24 then covered, leaving a bare pole) is gone; the clump keeps its blocked cells.",
